\\\": false, \\\"unscored\\\": true}, \\\"sensationalism\\\": {\\\"headline_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"body_score\\\": 6.6, \\\"clickbait_signals\\\": 0, \\\"superlative_density\\\": 0.0, \\\"urgency_density\\\": 0.0, \\\"hyperbole_density\\\": 0.0, \\\"measured_density\\\": 0.0, \\\"partisan_attack_density\\\": 0.0}, \\\"opinion\\\": {\\\"pronoun_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"subjectivity_score\\\": 23.6, \\\"modal_score\\\": 3.7, \\\"hedging_score\\\": 4.7, \\\"attribution_score\\\": 22.0, \\\"metadata_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"value_judgment_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"absolutist_assertion_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"classification\\\": \\\"Reporting\\\", \\\"dominant_signals\\\": [\\\"subjectivity\\\", \\\"attribution_gaps\\\", \\\"modal_language\\\"]}, \\\"coverage\\\": {\\\"named_sources_count\\\": 3, \\\"org_citations_count\\\": 4, \\\"data_points_count\\\": 0, \\\"direct_quotes_count\\\": 7, \\\"vague_sources_count\\\": 0, \\\"specificity_ratio\\\": 0.0}, \\\"framing\\\": {\\\"connotation_score\\\": 16.0, \\\"keyword_emphasis_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"omission_score\\\": 40.0, \\\"headline_body_divergence\\\": 2.1, \\\"has_cluster_context\\\": true}}\""}]}}, {"article": {"id": "8e9e7dc4-3c5a-4a82-b38c-9f6dfda6b71e", "title": "‘Uniform Means Uniform’: Allahabad High Court dismisses Muslim girl’s plea to wear Hijab with school uniform", "url": "https://organiser.org/2026/08/25/376902/bharat/uniform-means-uniform-allahabad-high-court-dismisses-muslim-girls-plea-to-wear-hijab-with-school-uniform/", "summary": "The constitutional, religious and educational debate surrounding the ‘hijab’ in the country has once again reached the doors of the court. The Allahabad High Court dismissed a petition filed by a minor Muslim student from Prayagraj, in which she had sought permission to wear a headscarf along with the prescribed school uniform. The court said that the petitioner had failed to present sufficient material to establish that wearing the hijab is an essential religious practice in Islam, without which the fundamental character of religious faith would be affected. The court also made it clear that if an educational institution’s dress policy is uniform, genuine, non-discriminatory and framed with the objective of maintaining discipline and institutional identity, a demand to alter the prescribed uniform cannot be accepted as a right. In fact, the matter came before a Division Bench comprising Justice J.J. Munir and Justice Indrajit Shukla on behalf of a student named Sukaina Rizvi. Sukai...", "published_at": "2026-08-25 09:00:57+00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Organiser", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://organiser.org"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 90, "sensationalism": 18, "opinion_fact": 29, "factual_rigor": 18, "framing": 15, "confidence": 0.52, "rationale": "\"{\\\"lean\\\": {\\\"keyword_score\\\": 50.0, \\\"framing_shift\\\": 0.0, \\\"entity_shift\\\": 0.0, \\\"sentence_direction\\\": 0.0, \\\"text_score\\\": 50.0, \\\"source_baseline\\\": 90, \\\"text_shift\\\": 0.0, \\\"delta_max\\\": 10, \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0, \\\"top_left_keywords\\\": [], \\\"top_right_keywords\\\": [], \\\"framing_phrases_found\\\": [], \\\"entity_sentiments\\\": {}, \\\"state_affiliated\\\": false, \\\"unscored\\\": false}, \\\"sensationalism\\\": {\\\"headline_score\\\": 1.6, \\\"body_score\\\": 7.1, \\\"clickbait_signals\\\": 0, \\\"superlative_density\\\": 0.0, \\\"urgency_density\\\": 0.0, \\\"hyperbole_density\\\": 0.0, \\\"measured_density\\\": 0.0, \\\"partisan_attack_density\\\": 0.0}, \\\"opinion\\\": {\\\"pronoun_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"subjectivity_score\\\": 21.5, \\\"modal_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"hedging_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"attribution_score\\\": 35.4, \\\"metadata_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"value_judgment_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"absolutist_assertion_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"classification\\\": \\\"Analysis\\\", \\\"dominant_signals\\\": [\\\"attribution_gaps\\\", \\\"subjectivity\\\"]}, \\\"coverage\\\": {\\\"named_sources_count\\\": 0, \\\"org_citations_count\\\": 1, \\\"data_points_count\\\": 0, \\\"direct_quotes_count\\\": 1, \\\"vague_sources_count\\\": 0, \\\"specificity_ratio\\\": 0.0}, \\\"framing\\\": {\\\"connotation_score\\\": 12.9, \\\"keyword_emphasis_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"omission_score\\\": 40.0, \\\"headline_body_divergence\\\": 22.3, \\\"has_cluster_context\\\": true}}\""}]}}, {"article": {"id": "962976a3-ce59-428e-bf9a-0572e86784a4", "title": "UP Raksha Bandhan 2026: Women, one companion can travel free by bus from August 27 night", "url": "https://organiser.org/2026/08/25/376923/bharat/up-raksha-bandhan-2026-women-one-companion-can-travel-free-by-bus-from-august-27-night/", "summary": "Lucknow – For many women, Raksha Bandhan is a chance to return home, meet their brothers and spend their time with families. With a large number of women expected to travel across Uttar Pradesh for Raksha Bandhan 2026, the state government is taking steps to make the journey safer and more comfortable. Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath announced free bus travel for women and one companion during Raksha Bandhan 2026. With passenger numbers expected to rise, the Uttar Pradesh Transport Department has ordered strict checks on buses, drivers, conductors, taxis and e-rickshaws. Transport Minister Dayashankar Singh has also directed the officials to ensure that UPSRTC buses are properly maintained and that all road safety rules are followed. Drivers and conductors will also be checked before starting their duty. Read More: ‘Uniform Means Uniform’: Allahabad High Court dismisses Muslim girl’s plea to wear Hijab with school uniform Drivers and conductors to undergo verification Private bus ope...", "published_at": "2026-08-25 09:40:03+00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Organiser", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://organiser.org"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 90, "sensationalism": 21, "opinion_fact": 30, "factual_rigor": 28, "framing": 30, "confidence": 0.54, "rationale": "\"{\\\"lean\\\": {\\\"keyword_score\\\": 50.0, \\\"fr